From 39c5ecd538ff8726f9ac84b0466050dd79c0fcce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sondre234 <sondrefmyrmel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 05:59:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] render, scene: add rounded clips and rounded rects

wlr_render_pass_set_rounding() shapes what a render pass draws next with an
anti-aliased rounded clip and an optional rounded hole (GLES2 only; other
renderers ignore it). The scene uses it for wlr_scene_tree_set_rounded_clip(),
which rounds everything below a tree, and wlr_scene_rect_set_rounding(), which
rounds a rect or reduces it to a rounded frame. Both are stored as node addons
so no public struct changes size.

The fragment shaders work the rounding out from the distances to the boxes'
edges, which the vertex shader computes. Small where they matter, these stay
precise at mediump, which NVIDIA runs the shaders at (it leaves
GL_FRAGMENT_PRECISION_HIGH undefined): buffer coordinates there lose the
fractions past 1024 px, which stair-stepped the corners.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
